-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fredoka and Nunito fonts

The drawn screens use Fredoka (Copyright 2016 The Fredoka Project Authors,
https://github.com/hafontia/Fredoka-One) and Nunito (Copyright 2014 The Nunito
Project Authors, https://github.com/googlefonts/nunito), from Google Fonts
(https://github.com/google/fonts). Both are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1,
see assets/fonts/fredoka/OFL.txt and assets/fonts/nunito/OFL.txt. The files in
assets/fonts are fixed-weight instances of the variable fonts (made with
fontTools), and the build turns a few sizes of them into glyph bitmaps that are
built into the 3DS app.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Button glyphs

The A, B, L, R and D-pad glyphs on the drawn screens come from Input Prompts by
Kenney (https://kenney.nl/assets/input-prompts), released under Creative
Commons Zero (CC0 1.0). The SVG files used and Kenney's license text are in
assets/buttons. The build rasterises and tints them for the 3DS app.

